 "answer_raw": "Amazon has a localized marketplace in **Brazil**, while other countries in South America primarily rely on **international shipping** or local alternatives [4].\n\nWhile many countries are eligible for **Amazon International Shipping**—allowing customers to order products from larger regional marketplaces—they do not have dedicated local storefronts [4]. In terms of localized iterations, **Brazil** is one of the few countries with its own specific marketplace in the region [4].\n\nI didn't find which local competitors or alternative services people use in other South American countries; you would need to check local e-commerce market share reports for those specifics.",
